1. A linear measuring apparatus (10), comprising:  

   a first body (12) and a second body (14) arranged for relative linear displacement along a measuring direction (X);  

   a scale band (16) mounted to the first body (12), the scale band (16) extending in the measuring direction (X) and having a marker pattern (18) formed thereon;  

   a sensing assembly (20) mounted to the second body (14), the sensing assembly (20) comprising a first sensor (22) and a second sensor (24) arranged to read respective portions of the marker pattern (18) during relative movement of the first body (12) and the second body (14);  

   wherein the marker pattern (18) comprises a plurality of stripes (26) distributed along the scale band (16), the plurality of stripes (26) defining a first trace (28) and a second trace (30) extending generally parallel to the measuring direction (X);  

   wherein each stripe (26) includes at least one transition edge (32) extending transversely across the first trace (28) and the second trace (30);  

   wherein the transition edges (32) of the marker pattern (18) are formed at respective inclination angles relative to the measuring direction (X), and wherein the inclination angles are selected such that successive transition edges (32) present a unique angular relationship across the first trace (28) and the second trace (30); and  

   wherein the first sensor (22) is positioned to detect the marker pattern (18) at the first trace (28), the second sensor (24) is positioned to detect the marker pattern (18) at the second trace (30), and signals generated by the first sensor (22) and the second sensor (24) are usable to identify an absolute or relative position of the scale band (16) with respect to the sensing assembly (20).
